      "speaker_id": "1995",
      "split": "test-clean",
      "text": "THE NET AND WEB OF ENDLESS THINGS HAD BEEN CRAWLING AND CREEPING AROUND HER SHE HAD STRUGGLED IN DUMB SPEECHLESS TERROR AGAINST SOME MIGHTY GRASPING THAT STROVE FOR HER LIFE WITH GNARLED AND CREEPING FINGERS BUT NOW AT LAST WEAKLY SHE OPENED HER EYES AND QUESTIONED",
      "utterance_id": "1995-1837-0023"
    },
    {
      "path": "/media/user/5bc0dc8d-c938-4b2a-af1b-94174fc511a9/datasets/revtrace/librispeech/LibriSpeech/test-clean/2094/142345/2094-142345-0002.flac",
